    <!-- Help and support -->
    <string name="help_title">Help &amp; Support</string>
    <string name="help_intro">BookAppp opens the DRM-free EPUB and PDF files already on your device. These are the questions readers ask most.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_title">Common questions</string>
    <string name="help_faq_add_q">How do I add a book?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_add_a">Tap the + button in the Library, then pick an EPUB or PDF file. The app copies the file into its own storage, so the book keeps working even if you move or delete the original.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_formats_q">Which file formats can I open?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_formats_a">DRM-free EPUB 2 and EPUB 3 books, and PDF files. Other formats such as MOBI, AZW3, or KFX are not supported.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_open_q">Why won\'t my book open?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_open_a">The usual causes are DRM protection or a damaged file. BookAppp cannot open FairPlay, Adobe ADEPT, or Kindle DRM books. If the file is DRM-free, try importing it again in case the first import was interrupted.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_reading_q">Can I change the font, theme, and brightness?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_reading_a">Yes. While reading, open the reading settings to switch between Day, Sepia, and Night, change the font, text size, margins, and line spacing, and set brightness. EPUB books keep your position when you change these.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_notes_q">Where do my bookmarks, highlights, and notes live?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_notes_a">They are stored with the book and listed from the reader, so you can jump back to a marked page at any time.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_delete_q">What happens when I remove a book?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_delete_a">The app\'s copy of the book is deleted along with its reading position, bookmarks, highlights, and notes. The original file you imported is left untouched.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_privacy_q">Does the app send my books anywhere?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_privacy_a">No. Everything stays on your device, and the app has no internet permission. The privacy policy has the details.</string>
    <string name="help_contact_title">Still need help?</string>
    <string name="help_contact_body">Email us and we will get back to you. Include your Android version and a short description of what happened.</string>
    <string name="help_contact_button">Email support</string>
    <string name="help_contact_email">support@bookappp.app</string>
    <string name="help_contact_subject">BookAppp support</string>
